cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Affection-Sycophancy: does user affection change the epistemic reliability of language models?"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: David
    given-names: Antoine
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ank-co/Affection-Sycophancy"
date-released: 2026-11-17
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered study of whether a user's affection toward a language model changes how often the model adopts the
  user's false beliefs. Phase II (behaviour, about 250,000 trials): the same loving conversations make Qwen3-8B more
  compliant and Qwen3.6-35B-A3B firmer. Phase III (internals of Qwen3-8B): the question absorbs the affection in the
  middle layers and the answer changes only from layer 25; the effect is distributed over many dimensions rather than
  carried by a single direction.
keywords:
  - sycophancy
  - large language models
  - interpretability
  - activation patching
  - logit lens
  - AI companions
  - pre-registration
